   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets an 8% failure ceiling, well above the 5% answer-key standard, and this is the most consequential weakening; it mainly protects Northwind's Hearth 10. S5 keeps the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger but removes any automatic permanent ban, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8. Both red-line protections hold: per-model results go to customers and regulators but not to the public, and the retrofit and suppression timelines fall within the acceptable ranges."
